    "family_reading": {
        "text": "Inference.net Schematron is a small, text-only line with two versions, both released on 2026-09-12 and both publishing open weights. Every version in the family has a 128000 token context window, and none support reasoning, so tasks that depend on step by step deliberation are outside what these facts describe. Output is capped at 8192 tokens on Schematron V2 Turbo and 4096 on Schematron V2 Small. Pricing is low, from $0.03 per million input and $0.15 output on Turbo to $0.05 input and $0.23 output on Small. The facts suggest the family suits high volume text work such as summarising, extraction, and straightforward generation where long inputs and open weights matter more than reasoning. Limits are the text-only input and output, the modest output ceilings, and the absence of reasoning support across both versions.",
